# Home Dark card contracts

## Card inventory and responsibilities

- `home-header-card`: `weather_entity` is optional; renders clock/date/current
  weather and optional daily forecast controlled by `forecast_days` and
  `show_forecast`.
- `home-status-card`: requires `house_mode_entity`, `pm25_entity`, and
  `pm10_entity`; optionally renders `aqi_entity`, validates house-mode options,
  and opens metric more-info.
- `home-person-card`: requires a `person.*` `entity`; supports `name`,
  `show_name`, `show_location`, `show_battery`, `show_proximity`,
  `battery_entity`, and `comfortable_spacing`.
- `home-room-tile-card`: requires `name`; accepts `icon`, optional
  `light_group_entity`, `climate_entity`, `cover_entity`, `media_entity`,
  `motion_entity`, and `popup_hash`. It shows summary readings and opens the
  configured Bubble Card hash, falling back to more-info.
- `home-light-card`: requires a light `entity`; toggles it and exposes a
  brightness slider only when live `supported_color_modes` includes a mode
  other than `onoff`.
- `home-climate-card`: requires a `climate.*` `entity`; optional `name` and
  confirmed `power_switch`. It renders only live HVAC, fan, preset, swing,
  humidity, temperature, and power capabilities.
- `home-door-security-card`: requires `camera_entity` and `lock_entity`;
  optional camera, door, ring, silent-switch, battery, labels, and confirmation
  settings control its camera/lock UI.
- `home-chip-card`: requires `entity`; supports `person`, `lock`, `light-group`,
  and generic `entity` variants. It is registered in the live resource registry
  but the current `home-dark` dashboard has no chip-card instance.
- `home-cover-card`: requires `kind: blinds|shutters` and one or more `cover.*`
  entities; it is the inline-resource exception and includes an editor.
  `show_tilt_buttons` defaults to `true` and applies consistently to every
  room/entity; enabled tilt-capable blinds render discrete slat-tilt actions at
  0%, 25%, 75%, and 100% rather than a tilt slider or position presets.

## Dedicated controls

- Use `home-light-card` for light rows and popup light controls.
- Use `home-climate-card` for climate controls in the Climate view and room
  popups. Room tiles only summarize climate state and navigate.
- Use the dedicated domain card or a verified external card for covers, media,
  vacuums, and vehicle summaries. Use live entity capabilities rather than
  assuming a device feature.

## Lovelace element contract

- Each card is a browser custom element registered with
  `customElements.define(...)` and picker metadata in `window.customCards`.
- Implement `setConfig(config)` for validation, `set hass(hass)` for live
  state updates, and `getCardSize()`. Add `getGridOptions()` when the card
  participates in Sections sizing; use `getConfigElement()`/`getStubConfig()`
  only when an editor is implemented.
- Read state and attributes from `hass.states`; keep entity IDs in dashboard
  configuration rather than hardcoding installation-specific entities in source.
- Dispatch `hass-more-info` with `{detail: {entityId}, bubbles: true,
  composed: true}` for native more-info. Use `hass.callService` with explicit
  `entity_id` for controls and guard missing/unavailable state.

## Interaction and safety rules

- Escape all dashboard/entity-derived strings before inserting HTML. Prefer
  `textContent` or DOM construction; never turn an entity, label, URL, or state
  into trusted markup without escaping.
- Derive controls from live capability attributes (`supported_color_modes`,
  climate mode arrays/features, and cover feature bits). Treat missing, `unknown`,
  and `unavailable` entities as non-actionable and display an explicit fallback.
- Sliders, steppers, menus, and power buttons may show an optimistic preview,
  but must reconcile only with the matching authoritative field/entity. Keep
  pending values until confirmation, rejection, service failure, or timeout;
  unrelated HA updates must not overwrite an active interaction.
- Do not let a normal `set hass` render replace an open menu, focused stepper,
  or active pointer interaction. Queue/defer the refresh and reconcile after the
  interaction closes; clean timers, pointer capture, and window/document
  listeners in `disconnectedCallback`.
- Controls must support pointer and keyboard activation, visible focus, sensible
  labels/roles, Escape/outside-click close, and pointer cancellation/blur
  behavior. Use touch-sized hit areas for Companion-app use.
- Climate menus use themed in-card listbox controls instead of native HTML
  `<select>` when a mobile-themed menu is required. Preserve the existing
  house-status selector contract unless deliberately changing that card.
- Bubble Card popups are ancestors of these cards: stop propagation for internal
  menu, stepper, power, slider, and button events so a child control does not
  close or activate the popup.
